; ==========================================================================
; STELLAR SIMPLE-CALC 8  -  eight significant digits; the arithmetic is
; native 1802 called by $F1 RUNMC                          (VM1 @ $4000)
; ==========================================================================
; Companion to Simple-Calc-5 (same keys, same rules, three more digits).
; Needs firmware with RUNMC $F1, PRINTSTR $C1 and GETSTR $C2; built and
; verified against V0061.30, and again against V0061.36 (2026-11-01).
;
;   > 1/7              = 0.14285714
;   > 123456.78*9      = 1111111     (1111111.02 to 8 digits)
;   > 2+3*4            = 20          left to right, like a pocket calculator
;   > *2               = 40          a line starting + * / uses the last answer
;   > -2.5*4           = -10         a leading - is a negative number
;   > 99999999*99999999 = 9.9999998E15
;   > 5/0              = Err         the last answer is kept
;   > 5!               = 120         n! for a whole number 0..69 (exact, rounded once)
;   > 2s               = 1.4142136   s (or S) the square root, correctly rounded
;   > F                every digit of n!; plain numbers, with no made-up 0s
;   > E                long answers as d.ddddddd E x again (as it starts)
;   Esc, or Enter on an empty line, quits.  x also means times.
;
; NUMBERS carry 8 significant digits and a decimal exponent; every result is
; the exact answer ROUNDED HALF-UP to 8 digits (so 1/3*3 = 0.99999999, as on a
; pocket calculator). Up to 9.9999999E99; smaller than 1E-99 becomes 0.
; Plain display for integers of up to 12 digits and up to 12 decimal places,
; d.ddddddd E x otherwise.
;
; THE SPLIT. The STELLAR program ($4000-$44BE) reads the line, keeps the
; running answer and prints. All the arithmetic is ONE native routine at
; $4800 (Firmware-Math/calc8_native.asm, 1204 bytes), entered with RUNMC $4800
; and an operation letter at $4D30: N (round a typed number), + - * /.
; Numbers are held ONE DECIMAL DIGIT PER BYTE, so the parser writes digits
; straight into the native work area and the printer reads them back - no
; binary/decimal conversion anywhere. The native code does schoolbook
; arithmetic that is exact up to one final rounding: add/subtract at the true
; alignment, a full 16-digit product, and long division to 10 digits.
;
; RECORDS (page $4D): NA $4D00 the running answer, NB $4D10 the number just
; typed, ANS $4D20 the last answer. 10 bytes each: sign, exponent+$80, eight
; digits (most significant first); value = digits x 10^exponent. $4D30
; operation, $4D31 status (0 ok, 1 divide by zero, 2 too big), $4D32-34 the
; parser's raw exponent/count/sign, $4D40 work area, $4D80/$4D90 divide.
; Input line at $4E00.
;
; RUNMC CONVENTION (see RUNMC-Test.lst / gol_native.asm): absolute address,
; return with D5, RA avoided, SEX R2 before returning. Inside, the native code
; calls its own subroutines through the firmware's SCRT (D4/D5); that touches
; only R2, R3, R6 and D. The longest native call (a divide) is ~25,000 1802
; instructions - about a tenth of a second - and does not yield to other VMs.
;
; VERIFICATION (real V0061.30 image, cold boot):
;   Firmware-Math/calc8_native_test.py - the native routine alone, 3018 random + hand cases vs the model, 0 wrong.
;   Firmware-Math/simplecalc8_verify.py - the whole program against an
;   exact-fraction model, character for character: 81 set lines + 400 random expressions, 0 wrong.
;
; HARDWARE-VERIFIED on the Elf2K, 2026-09-24, on firmware V0061.33 - Craig: "works
; very well". The first app whose arithmetic runs as native 1802 through RUNMC.
; 2026-11-01: ! (factorial, exact digits worked out natively at $4F80, as
; SC/examples/fact.sc does), s (square root, digit by digit, native) and the
; F / E display setting - simulator-verified; not yet run on the Elf2K.
;
; 403 STELLAR commands, $4000-$44BE (1215 bytes); native code $4800-$4CB3.
;
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DISASSEMBLY  -  commented out; the loader skips it
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

; D 4000 CD             START                              Start of program, and run the label pre-pass
; D 4001 11 0F 00 0A    LOADXI R15 000A                    Ten
; D 4005 11 0E 0D 20    LOADXI R14 0D20                    The last answer starts as +0: sign 0, exponent $80,
; D 4009 32 0E 00 80    COPYMX2I R14 0080
; D 400D 52 0E 00 02    ADDXI R14 0002
; D 4011 32 0E 00 00    COPYMX2I R14 0000
; D 4015 52 0E 00 02    ADDXI R14 0002
; D 4019 32 0E 00 00    COPYMX2I R14 0000
; D 401D 52 0E 00 02    ADDXI R14 0002
; D 4021 32 0E 00 00    COPYMX2I R14 0000
; D 4025 52 0E 00 02    ADDXI R14 0002
; D 4029 32 0E 00 00    COPYMX2I R14 0000                  eight zero digits (the pre-pass does not clear RAM)
; D 402D 11 0E 00 00    LOADXI R14 0000
; D 4031 10 00 00       LOADAI 0000
; D 4034 2F 0E 0D 3F    WRITEIDX R14 0D3F                  E form to start with
; D 4038 2F 0E 0D 3B    WRITEIDX R14 0D3B
; D 403C 11 0E 06 70    LOADXI R14 0670
; D 4040 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14                       The banner
; PROMPT:
; D 4042 11 0E 00 00    LOADXI R14 0000
; D 4046 10 00 00       LOADAI 0000
; D 4049 2F 0E 0D 3D    WRITEIDX R14 0D3D                  no exact n! to show yet
; D 404D 11 0E 06 40    LOADXI R14 0640
; D 4051 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14                       >
; D 4053 11 0C 0E 00    LOADXI R12 0E00
; D 4057 11 0D 0E 00    LOADXI R13 0E00
; D 405B BD 02 9F       CALL GETL                          Read a line (echoed; backspace works; a lone ESC first quits)
; D 405E 11 0C 0E 00    LOADXI R12 0E00                    Back to the start of it
; D 4062 BD 02 F4       CALL SKIPSP
; D 4065 8C 00          TESTXZ R0                          An empty line quits
; D 4067 A0 02 98       IFTRUEI QUIT
; D 406A 11 05 00 00    LOADXI R5 0000                     F: every digit from now on
; D 406E 86 00 00 46    TESTXI R0 0046
; D 4072 A0 02 02       IFTRUEI MODE
; D 4075 86 00 00 66    TESTXI R0 0066
; D 4079 A0 02 02       IFTRUEI MODE
; D 407C 11 05 00 01    LOADXI R5 0001                     E: long answers in E form
; D 4080 86 00 00 45    TESTXI R0 0045
; D 4084 A0 02 02       IFTRUEI MODE
; D 4087 86 00 00 65    TESTXI R0 0065
; D 408B A0 02 02       IFTRUEI MODE
; D 408E 86 00 00 2B    TESTXI R0 002B                     A line that starts with + * / carries on
; D 4092 A0 00 D4       IFTRUEI USEANS
; D 4095 86 00 00 2A    TESTXI R0 002A                     from the last answer
; D 4099 A0 00 D4       IFTRUEI USEANS
; D 409C 86 00 00 2F    TESTXI R0 002F
; D 40A0 A0 00 D4       IFTRUEI USEANS
; D 40A3 86 00 00 21    TESTXI R0 0021                     and so does ! or s
; D 40A7 A0 00 D4       IFTRUEI USEANS
; D 40AA 86 00 00 73    TESTXI R0 0073
; D 40AE A0 00 D4       IFTRUEI USEANS
; D 40B1 86 00 00 53    TESTXI R0 0053
; D 40B5 A0 00 D4       IFTRUEI USEANS
; D 40B8 BD 03 15       CALL PARSE                         The first number -> NB
; D 40BB 8C 0A          TESTXZ R10                         No digits: not a number
; D 40BD A0 02 80       IFTRUEI SYNERR
; D 40C0 BD 03 08       CALL STATUS                        Too big to hold?
; D 40C3 A1 02 89       IFFALSEI MATHERR
; D 40C6 11 0D 0D 10    LOADXI R13 0D10                    It becomes the running answer NA
; D 40CA 11 0E 0D 00    LOADXI R14 0D00
; D 40CE 3B DE 0A       COPYMXMY R13 R14 0A                10-byte record
; D 40D1 B0 00 DF       GAL OPLOOP
; USEANS:
; D 40D4 11 0D 0D 20    LOADXI R13 0D20                    Load the last answer
; D 40D8 11 0E 0D 00    LOADXI R14 0D00
; D 40DC 3B DE 0A       COPYMXMY R13 R14 0A                10-byte record
; OPLOOP:
; D 40DF BD 02 F4       CALL SKIPSP
; D 40E2 8C 00          TESTXZ R0                          End of the line: show the answer
; D 40E4 A0 02 35       IFTRUEI SHOW
; D 40E7 23 00 09       COPYXY R0 -> R9                    R9 = the operator
; D 40EA 86 09 00 21    TESTXI R9 0021                     ! and s act on the answer so far
; D 40EE A0 01 68       IFTRUEI FACT
; D 40F1 86 09 00 73    TESTXI R9 0073
; D 40F5 A0 01 4F       IFTRUEI SQRT
; D 40F8 86 09 00 53    TESTXI R9 0053
; D 40FC A0 01 4F       IFTRUEI SQRT
; D 40FF 86 09 00 2B    TESTXI R9 002B
; D 4103 A0 01 26       IFTRUEI OPOK
; D 4106 86 09 00 2D    TESTXI R9 002D
; D 410A A0 01 26       IFTRUEI OPOK
; D 410D 86 09 00 2A    TESTXI R9 002A
; D 4111 A0 01 26       IFTRUEI OPOK
; D 4114 86 09 00 2F    TESTXI R9 002F
; D 4118 A0 01 26       IFTRUEI OPOK
; D 411B 86 09 00 78    TESTXI R9 0078                     x means times
; D 411F A1 02 80       IFFALSEI SYNERR
; D 4122 11 09 00 2A    LOADXI R9 002A
; OPOK:
; D 4126 42 0C          INCX R12                           Past the operator
; D 4128 BD 02 F4       CALL SKIPSP
; D 412B BD 03 15       CALL PARSE                         The next number -> NB
; D 412E 8C 0A          TESTXZ R10
; D 4130 A0 02 80       IFTRUEI SYNERR
; D 4133 BD 03 08       CALL STATUS
; D 4136 A1 02 89       IFFALSEI MATHERR
; D 4139 11 0E 00 00    LOADXI R14 0000
; D 413D 22 09          COPYXA R9 -> Acc                   The operation letter for the native code
; D 413F 2F 0E 0D 30    WRITEIDX R14 0D30
; D 4143 F1 48 00       RUNMC 4800                         NA = NA op NB, in raw 1802
; D 4146 BD 03 08       CALL STATUS                        Divide by zero, or too big?
; D 4149 A1 02 89       IFFALSEI MATHERR
; D 414C B0 00 DF       GAL OPLOOP
; SQRT:
; D 414F 42 0C          INCX R12                           Past the s
; D 4151 11 0E 00 00    LOADXI R14 0000
; D 4155 10 00 52       LOADAI 0052
; D 4158 2F 0E 0D 30    WRITEIDX R14 0D30
; D 415C F1 48 00       RUNMC 4800                         NA = the square root of NA
; D 415F BD 03 08       CALL STATUS                        A negative number has none
; D 4162 A1 02 89       IFFALSEI MATHERR
; D 4165 B0 00 DF       GAL OPLOOP
; FACT:
; D 4168 42 0C          INCX R12                           Past the !
; D 416A 11 0E 00 00    LOADXI R14 0000
; D 416E 11 07 00 00    LOADXI R7 0000                     n = 0
; D 4172 2E 0E 0D 02    READIDX R14 0D02                   NA is 0: 0! = 1
; D 4176 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000
; D 4179 A0 01 D0       IFTRUEI FGO
; D 417C 2E 0E 0D 00    READIDX R14 0D00                   Negative: Err
; D 4180 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000
; D 4183 A1 02 89       IFFALSEI MATHERR
; D 4186 2E 0E 0D 01    READIDX R14 0D01
; D 418A 21 05          COPYAX Acc -> R5                   R5 = e + $80
; D 418C 11 04 00 01    LOADXI R4 0001                     One digit before the point (e = -7)
; D 4190 86 05 00 79    TESTXI R5 0079
; D 4194 A0 01 A2       IFTRUEI FDIG
; D 4197 11 04 00 02    LOADXI R4 0002                     Two (e = -6); any other e: a fraction, or 100 and up
; D 419B 86 05 00 7A    TESTXI R5 007A
; D 419F A1 02 89       IFFALSEI MATHERR
; FDIG:
; D 41A2 11 08 00 00    LOADXI R8 0000                     n = those digits
; FD1:
; D 41A6 4A 7F          MULTXY R7 * R15
; D 41A8 21 17          COPYAX MA -> R7
; D 41AA 2E 08 0D 02    READIDX R8 0D02
; D 41AE 21 05          COPYAX Acc -> R5
; D 41B0 50 75 07       ADDXYZ R7 + R5 -> R7
; D 41B3 42 08          INCX R8
; D 41B5 87 84          TESTXY R8 = R4
; D 41B7 A1 01 A6       IFFALSEI FD1
; FD2:
; D 41BA 86 08 00 08    TESTXI R8 0008
; D 41BE A0 01 D0       IFTRUEI FGO
; D 41C1 2E 08 0D 02    READIDX R8 0D02
; D 41C5 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000
; D 41C8 A1 02 89       IFFALSEI MATHERR
; D 41CB 42 08          INCX R8
; D 41CD B0 01 BA       GAL FD2
; FGO:
; D 41D0 11 05 00 45    LOADXI R5 0045                     70! and up do not fit: Err
; D 41D4 88 57          TESTGXY R5 >= R7
; D 41D6 A1 02 89       IFFALSEI MATHERR
; D 41D9 22 07          COPYXA R7 -> Acc
; D 41DB 2F 0E 0D 3E    WRITEIDX R14 0D3E
; D 41DF 10 00 00       LOADAI 0000
; D 41E2 2F 0E 0D 3B    WRITEIDX R14 0D3B                  BIG changes: it no longer holds the last answer
; D 41E6 10 00 58       LOADAI 0058
; D 41E9 2F 0E 0D 30    WRITEIDX R14 0D30
; D 41ED F1 48 00       RUNMC 4800                         n! exactly into BIG, and NA = it rounded to 8 digits
; D 41F0 BD 02 F4       CALL SKIPSP                        The ! ends the line: the answer is n! exactly
; D 41F3 8C 00          TESTXZ R0
; D 41F5 A1 00 DF       IFFALSEI OPLOOP
; D 41F8 10 00 01       LOADAI 0001
; D 41FB 2F 0E 0D 3D    WRITEIDX R14 0D3D
; D 41FF B0 00 DF       GAL OPLOOP
; MODE:
; D 4202 42 0C          INCX R12
; D 4204 BD 02 F4       CALL SKIPSP
; D 4207 8C 00          TESTXZ R0
; D 4209 A1 02 80       IFFALSEI SYNERR
; D 420C 11 0E 00 00    LOADXI R14 0000
; D 4210 22 05          COPYXA R5 -> Acc
; D 4212 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000
; D 4215 10 00 01       LOADAI 0001
; D 4218 A0 02 1E       IFTRUEI MODE1
; D 421B 10 00 00       LOADAI 0000
; MODE1:
; D 421E 2F 0E 0D 3F    WRITEIDX R14 0D3F
; D 4222 2E 0E 0D 3B    READIDX R14 0D3B                   the last answer, exact if it was n!
; D 4226 2F 0E 0D 3D    WRITEIDX R14 0D3D
; D 422A 11 0D 0D 20    LOADXI R13 0D20
; D 422E 11 0E 0D 00    LOADXI R14 0D00
; D 4232 3B DE 0A       COPYMXMY R13 R14 0A                10-byte record
; SHOW:
; D 4235 11 0D 0D 00    LOADXI R13 0D00                    Keep it as the last answer
; D 4239 11 0E 0D 20    LOADXI R14 0D20
; D 423D 3B DE 0A       COPYMXMY R13 R14 0A                10-byte record
; D 4240 11 0E 06 48    LOADXI R14 0648
; D 4244 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14                        =
; D 4246 11 0E 00 00    LOADXI R14 0000
; D 424A 2E 0E 0D 3D    READIDX R14 0D3D                   This answer an exact n!?
; D 424E 2F 0E 0D 3B    WRITEIDX R14 0D3B                  (remembered for F)
; D 4252 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000
; D 4255 A0 02 62       IFTRUEI SHOWN
; D 4258 2E 0E 0D 3F    READIDX R14 0D3F                   and F on: every digit
; D 425C 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000
; D 425F A1 02 68       IFFALSEI SHOWX
; SHOWN:
; D 4262 BD 03 BA       CALL PRINTNUM
; D 4265 B0 00 42       GAL PROMPT
; SHOWX:
; D 4268 2E 0E 0D 3C    READIDX R14 0D3C
; D 426C 21 04          COPYAX Acc -> R4
; SHX1:
; D 426E 43 04          DECX R4
; D 4270 2E 04 0F 80    READIDX R4 0F80
; D 4274 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 4277 C9             SEROUT
; D 4278 8C 04          TESTXZ R4
; D 427A A1 02 6E       IFFALSEI SHX1
; D 427D B0 00 42       GAL PROMPT
; SYNERR:
; D 4280 11 0E 06 58    LOADXI R14 0658
; D 4284 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14                        = ?  (the last answer is kept)
; D 4286 B0 00 42       GAL PROMPT
; MATHERR:
; D 4289 11 0E 06 48    LOADXI R14 0648
; D 428D C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 428F 11 0E 06 50    LOADXI R14 0650
; D 4293 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14                       Err
; D 4295 B0 00 42       GAL PROMPT
; QUIT:
; D 4298 11 0E 06 60    LOADXI R14 0660
; D 429C C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 429E 00             HALT
; GETL:
; GETLK:
; D 429F CB             SERIN                              the first key
; D 42A0 81 00 1B       TESTAI 001B
; D 42A3 A1 02 B7       IFFALSEI GETLN
; D 42A6 BD 02 DB       CALL GETLW                         ESC: an arrow following?
; D 42A9 A1 02 98       IFFALSEI QUIT                      no: ESC on its own quits
; D 42AC CB             SERIN                              an arrow (ESC [ x): its two bytes are thrown away
; D 42AD BD 02 DB       CALL GETLW
; D 42B0 A1 02 9F       IFFALSEI GETLK
; D 42B3 CB             SERIN
; D 42B4 B0 02 9F       GAL GETLK
; GETLN:
; D 42B7 81 00 0D       TESTAI 000D
; D 42BA A1 02 C5       IFFALSEI GETLC
; D 42BD 10 00 00       LOADAI 0000
; D 42C0 36 01 0C       COPYIAMX 1 byte Acc -> M(R12)      Enter alone: the empty line
; D 42C3 BE 00          RETURN
; GETLC:
; D 42C5 81 00 08       TESTAI 0008
; D 42C8 A0 02 9F       IFTRUEI GETLK                      nothing to rub out yet
; D 42CB 81 00 7F       TESTAI 007F
; D 42CE A0 02 9F       IFTRUEI GETLK
; D 42D1 C9             SEROUT                             the echo
; D 42D2 36 01 0C       COPYIAMX 1 byte Acc -> M(R12)
; D 42D5 42 0C          INCX R12
; D 42D7 C2 CD          GETSTR R12 R13                     the rest of the line (Backspace can rub out the first key too)
; D 42D9 BE 00          RETURN
; GETLW:
; D 42DB 72 09          PUSHX R9
; D 42DD 11 09 00 08    LOADXI R9 0008
; GETLW1:
; D 42E1 CC             SERST
; D 42E2 A0 02 EC       IFTRUEI GETLW2
; D 42E5 43 09          DECX R9
; D 42E7 8C 09          TESTXZ R9
; D 42E9 A1 02 E1       IFFALSEI GETLW1
; GETLW2:
; D 42EC 73 09          POPX R9
; D 42EE CC             SERST                              Test: a key is waiting
; D 42EF BE 00          RETURN
; D 42F1 F0 00 00       BREAK                              End of program
; SKIPSP:
; D 42F4 2E 0C 00 00    READIDX R12 0000
; D 42F8 21 00          COPYAX Acc -> R0
; D 42FA 86 00 00 20    TESTXI R0 0020
; D 42FE A1 03 06       IFFALSEI SKR
; D 4301 42 0C          INCX R12
; D 4303 B0 02 F4       GAL SKIPSP
; SKR:
; D 4306 BE 00          RETURN
; STATUS:
; D 4308 11 0E 00 00    LOADXI R14 0000
; D 430C 2E 0E 0D 31    READIDX R14 0D31
; D 4310 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000
; D 4313 BE 00          RETURN
; PARSE:
; D 4315 11 04 00 00    LOADXI R4 0000
; D 4319 11 05 00 00    LOADXI R5 0000
; D 431D 11 06 00 80    LOADXI R6 0080
; D 4321 11 08 00 00    LOADXI R8 0000
; D 4325 11 0A 00 00    LOADXI R10 0000
; D 4329 2E 0C 00 00    READIDX R12 0000
; D 432D 21 00          COPYAX Acc -> R0
; D 432F 86 00 00 2D    TESTXI R0 002D                     A leading minus
; D 4333 A1 03 3C       IFFALSEI PLOOP
; D 4336 11 04 00 01    LOADXI R4 0001
; D 433A 42 0C          INCX R12
; PLOOP:
; D 433C 2E 0C 00 00    READIDX R12 0000
; D 4340 21 00          COPYAX Acc -> R0
; D 4342 86 00 00 2E    TESTXI R0 002E
; D 4346 A1 03 57       IFFALSEI PDIG
; D 4349 8C 08          TESTXZ R8                          A second point ends the number
; D 434B A1 03 98       IFFALSEI PEND
; D 434E 11 08 00 01    LOADXI R8 0001                     Digits from here on are fraction
; D 4352 42 0C          INCX R12
; D 4354 B0 03 3C       GAL PLOOP
; PDIG:
; D 4357 53 00 00 30    SUBXI R0 0030                      A digit is '0'..'9': c-'0' < 10
; D 435B 89 0F          TESTLXY R0 < R15
; D 435D A1 03 98       IFFALSEI PEND
; D 4360 42 0C          INCX R12
; D 4362 11 0A 00 01    LOADXI R10 0001                    Seen a digit
; D 4366 8C 05          TESTXZ R5                          A leading zero is not kept
; D 4368 A1 03 73       IFFALSEI PKEEP
; D 436B 8C 00          TESTXZ R0
; D 436D A1 03 73       IFFALSEI PKEEP
; D 4370 B0 03 84       GAL PFRAC                          but after the point it still moves the exponent
; PKEEP:
; D 4373 11 0E 00 14    LOADXI R14 0014                    Keep up to 20 digits
; D 4377 89 5E          TESTLXY R5 < R14
; D 4379 A1 03 8E       IFFALSEI PFULL
; D 437C 22 00          COPYXA R0 -> Acc
; D 437E 2F 05 0D 40    WRITEIDX R5 0D40                   W[k] = the digit
; D 4382 42 05          INCX R5
; PFRAC:
; D 4384 8C 08          TESTXZ R8                          After the point each digit is a tenth
; D 4386 A0 03 3C       IFTRUEI PLOOP
; D 4389 43 06          DECX R6
; D 438B B0 03 3C       GAL PLOOP
; PFULL:
; D 438E 8C 08          TESTXZ R8                          A dropped digit before the point is a x10
; D 4390 A1 03 3C       IFFALSEI PLOOP
; D 4393 42 06          INCX R6
; D 4395 B0 03 3C       GAL PLOOP
; PEND:
; D 4398 11 0E 00 00    LOADXI R14 0000                    Hand the raw digits to the native code
; D 439C 22 05          COPYXA R5 -> Acc
; D 439E 2F 0E 0D 33    WRITEIDX R14 0D33
; D 43A2 22 06          COPYXA R6 -> Acc
; D 43A4 2F 0E 0D 32    WRITEIDX R14 0D32
; D 43A8 22 04          COPYXA R4 -> Acc
; D 43AA 2F 0E 0D 34    WRITEIDX R14 0D34
; D 43AE 10 00 4E       LOADAI 004E
; D 43B1 2F 0E 0D 30    WRITEIDX R14 0D30
; D 43B5 F1 48 00       RUNMC 4800                         Round to 8 digits -> NB
; D 43B8 BE 00          RETURN
; PRINTNUM:
; D 43BA 11 07 00 08    LOADXI R7 0008
; PNT:
; D 43BE 8C 07          TESTXZ R7                          All eight zero: the number is 0
; D 43C0 A0 04 BB       IFTRUEI PNZERO
; D 43C3 43 07          DECX R7
; D 43C5 2E 07 0D 02    READIDX R7 0D02                    Drop trailing zeros
; D 43C9 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000
; D 43CC A0 03 BE       IFTRUEI PNT
; D 43CF 42 07          INCX R7
; D 43D1 11 0E 00 00    LOADXI R14 0000
; D 43D5 2E 0E 0D 00    READIDX R14 0D00                   The sign
; D 43D9 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000
; D 43DC A0 03 E1       IFTRUEI PN1
; D 43DF CA 2D          SEROUTI 2D '-'
; PN1:
; D 43E1 2E 0E 0D 01    READIDX R14 0D01                   e = exponent + 8 - n
; D 43E5 21 03          COPYAX Acc -> R3
; D 43E7 52 03 00 08    ADDXI R3 0008
; D 43EB 51 37 03       SUBXYZ R3 - R7 -> R3
; D 43EE 50 73 08       ADDXYZ R7 + R3 -> R8               p = n + e
; D 43F1 11 06 00 00    LOADXI R6 0000
; D 43F5 2E 0E 0D 3F    READIDX R14 0D3F                   F: plain, every digit - but only digits it knows:
; D 43F9 81 00 00       TESTAI 0000
; D 43FC A0 04 0B       IFTRUEI PNAUTO
; D 43FF 11 0E 00 88    LOADXI R14 0088                    more than 8 before the point would be made-up 0s,
; D 4403 88 E8          TESTGXY R14 >= R8
; D 4405 A0 04 34       IFTRUEI PNFMT
; D 4408 B0 04 29       GAL PNSCI                          so that one goes in E form
; PNAUTO:
; D 440B 11 0E 00 80    LOADXI R14 0080
; D 440F 88 3E          TESTGXY R3 >= R14                  e >= 0: plain if p <= 12
; D 4411 A1 04 20       IFFALSEI PNNEG
; D 4414 11 0E 00 8C    LOADXI R14 008C
; D 4418 88 E8          TESTGXY R14 >= R8
; D 441A A0 04 34       IFTRUEI PNFMT
; D 441D B0 04 29       GAL PNSCI
; PNNEG:
; D 4420 11 0E 00 74    LOADXI R14 0074                    e < 0: plain if e >= -12
; D 4424 88 3E          TESTGXY R3 >= R14
; D 4426 A0 04 34       IFTRUEI PNFMT
; PNSCI:
; D 4429 11 06 00 01    LOADXI R6 0001                     Otherwise d.ddddddd E x
; D 442D 23 00 89       COPYXY R8 -> R9
